        "Four floors, set behind a driveway long enough that guests arriving at night can watch the house grow from a distant light to a wall of stone before they ever reach the door. The ground floor holds the kitchen and the dining hall, the staff quarters tucked discreetly behind the main staircase where they can be summoned and forgotten in the same breath, trained to see nothing, hear nothing, repeat nothing, a discretion I pay for generously and enforce absolutely. The first floor is all office, every trace of my father's version of this life stripped from those walls the year I finally made the house entirely mine.",
